---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro'

// https://docs.astro.build/en/recipes/dynamically-importing-images/
const paintings = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('../assets/paintings/*.jpg')
---

<PageLayout title="Art">
  <div class="artPage">
    <div class="paintings">

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Blue Jay'
          class="painting"
          priority
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/blue-jay.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Blue Jay</div>
        <div class="date">2019 • 8×10″ • $400</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Barn Swallow'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/barn-swallow.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Barn Swallow</div>
        <div class="date">2019 • 8×10″ • Sold</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Baltimore Oriole'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/baltimore-oriole.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Baltimore Oriole</div>
        <div class="date">2019 • 8×10″ • Sold</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Purple Finch'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/purple-finch.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Purple Finch</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • Sold</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Cardinal'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/cardinal.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Cardinal</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • Sold</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Tufted Titmouse'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/titmouse.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Tufted Titmouse</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • $300</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Bluebird'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/bluebird.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Bluebird</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • Sold</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Sparrow'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/sparrow.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Sparrow</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • $300</div>
      </div>

      <div class="paintingCell">
        <Image
          alt='Painting of a Goldfinch'
          class="painting"
          src={ paintings['../assets/paintings/goldfinch.jpg']() }
        />
        <div class="title">Goldfinch</div>
        <div class="date">2018 • 8×10″ • $200</div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="words">
      <h2 class="wordsHeader">About the Birds series</h2>
      <p>
        When I was a child, I was fascinated by my mother's <em>Birds of North
        America</em> field guide. She kept it on the top shelf of a bookcase in
        our living room, but that didn't stop me from pulling it down and flipping
        through it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I spent a great deal of time looking at birds I recognized (and many I didn't).
        Occasionally, when we saw a new bird at the feeder or on the locust tree
        in the back yard, Mom would pull the book down and we'd look together until
        we identified it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is undoubtedly a family obsession. During my childhood trips to visit
        my grandparents in Florida, neither my grandma nor my grandpa ever missed
        the opportunity to point out the local bird life. It's entirely thanks to
        my mother and grandparents that I'm able to identify pretty much any bird
        who hops across the sidewalk.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each of the birds I've painted in this series has a special memory
        associated with it. The goldfinch and purple finch are regular guests at
        my Mom's birdfeeders. The sparrow reminds me of the one I rescued from a
        light fixture and rehabilitated in my laundry room. The first titmouse I
        spotted was courtesy of my grandma in Michigan one summer. The bluebird is
        an homage to my grandma, who remains alive in my memory as one of the
        kindest, most vibrant women I've ever known.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</PageLayout>


<style>
  .artPage {
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-top: var(--page-top-padding);
    max-width: 500px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .paintings {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .paintingCell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 5px 5px;
    width: 48%;
  }

  .paintingCell img {
    height: auto;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .title {
    display: flex;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 5px 0 0 0;
  }

  .date {
    color: #999;
    font-size: 13px;
    /* font-style: italic; */
  }

  .words {
    margin: 25px 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 500px) {
    .words {
      padding: 0 25px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .artPage {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      max-width: 90%;
    }

    .paintings {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
      width: 50%;
    }

    .paintingCell {
      margin: 5px 2.5%;
      width: 40%;
    }

    .words {
      margin-top: 0;
      width: 600px;
    }

    .wordsHeader {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }
</style>
